// NEGATIVE TEST -- N2-11. An unknown attribute is a COMPILE ERROR.
//
// This is the row the attribute surface exists to protect. `#` lexes (N2-10),
// so `#[frobnicate]` is read all the way to a name; nothing implements it, so
// it is refused, and the diagnostic NAMES it.
//
// The alternative -- lex it, shrug, generate code -- is the defect class M1
// was spent deleting, one construct along: a source file that requests a
// property and a binary that does not have it, with no diagnostic in between.
// Every attribute is refused today because `KNOWN_ATTRIBUTES` is empty, and
// that emptiness is the correct M2 state rather than an oversight: the only
// attribute the specification names is `#[total]` (N8), which M6 owns, and a
// compiler that accepts an obligation it cannot discharge is worse than one
// that says no.
#[frobnicate]
fn f() -> i64 {
    return 1;
}

fn main() {
    print_int(f());
}
